      "finding": "SAMPLER-011 actually selects A, edits Detune and selects B. It expects the Sample chooser/editor display to follow that selection, but does not state that either selection is performed through the Sample chooser. The audit wrongly calls this an actual chooser action, most explicitly sampler:B078: actuallychangeseditedlayer viachoosertrue. An implementation with correct layer-list focus/display but a broken Sample chooser entrypoint could satisfy the stated case action. This is an audit association overstatement, not evidence of wrong application behavior or a contradiction in the old owner.",
      "requested_minimal_correction": "Preserve all original owner/source/case bytes and the genuine per-layer Detune/focus and expected chooser-display subset. In a preserved audit successor, narrow the two assessments to that subset; do not call it chooser invocation. G18 already proposes actual Samplechooser, so retain that concrete proposal and explicitly route B078 to it or leave invocation documented-but-unexercised/U. Do not invent a chooser gesture, new runtime oracle, requirement ID or coverage credit.",
      "verification_expectation": "Rebuild the versioned audit after minimal plan changes; add a focused guard/unsafe fixture rejecting promotion of expected chooser display or generic select-A/select-B action into a chooser invocation. The old case and input pins remain exact.",
