      ],
      "source": {
        "local_block": "simpler:B040",
        "pointer": "/blocks/259/text",
        "quote": "The Warp as… button adjusts the warping of the sample so that it will play back precisely within the specified number of bars or beats. Live makes its best guess about what this value should be based on the length of the sample, but if it gets it wrong, you can use the ÷2 or ×2 buttons to double or halve the playback speed, respectively."
      },
      "audit_claims": [
        {
          "pointer": "/assessments/259/assessment",
          "text": "018actualWarpas/÷2thenreset×2true; bestguessnotconstructor/samplingformula. Source÷2doublespeed×2halves preservedwithouttimingoracle."
        },
        {
          "pointer": "/proposals/6/proposed_minimal_delta",
          "text": "Preserve018actualWarpas/÷2/reset×2. Propose independently productive two-pitch histories withWarpOFF andWarpON atmatchedtempo, then separately changeSettempo ineach admittedmode."
        }
      ],
      "actual_selected_case": {
        "pointer": "/owner_cases/17",
        "id": "SIMPLER-018",
        "setup": "Neutral pitch, Warp as 2 bars at 120 BPM, full 4-second sample.",
        "action": "Choose ÷2 then reset and choose ×2.",
        "expected": "÷2 doubles speed and ×2 halves speed relative to that setup; exact interpolation ungraded."
      },
      "finding": "SIMPLER-018 supplies a Warp-as-2-bars setup and actually chooses division-by-two, resets and chooses multiplication-by-two. It does not explicitly invoke the Warp as button. A260 and G07 promote that setup to an actual Warp-as invocation; G07 then omits the command from its missing-action proposal. The genuine known setup and division/multiplication actions remain valid and must be retained.",
      "requested_minimal_correction": "In a preserved audit successor, distinguish the known Warp-as setup from the actual division/multiplication commands. Narrow A260/G07 and retain the source button role as documented-but-unexercised/U, or add an explicit admitted Warp as button invocation to the existing bounded G07 future proposal. Use an independently admitted NONEMPTY productive sample/Warp context for any effect comparison; keep documentary/actual numeric, timing and signal oracles null. No old owner/case rewrite, new normative ID, tempo formula or whole-group completion.",
      "verification_expectation": "A focused association fixture must reject using setup text alone as proof that a particular command was invoked. Preserve all original SIMPLER-018 fields and source bytes; check only the minimal successor delta and resulting reverse group mappings.",
